[0m[48;2;15;18;22m Write a haiku about tide charts, then explain it in [0m
[0m[48;2;15;18;22m three sentences.                                    [0m
[0m[48;2;15;18;22m                                                     [0m

 Tides rise and fall slow,                           
 Moon pulls the ocean's great breath,                
 Time marks the rhythm.                              
                                                     
 This haiku captures the cyclical nature of tides,   
 which are governed by the gravitational pull of the 
 moon on Earth's oceans. The "great breath" metaphor 
 suggests the rhythmic, almost living quality of     
 tidal movements as water rises and falls in         
 predictable patterns. Tide charts document this     
 ancient celestial dance, allowing us to read and    
 predict the ocean's movements across time.          

